Distinguish observed facts from assumptions. Avoid declaring an incident confirmed unless the evidence supports that conclusion.

## 💡 6. SOC Interview Questions

**Q1. What is Windows Event ID 4624?**

It records a successful logon when the relevant event is generated and available in the Security log.

**Q2. What is the difference between Event IDs 4624 and 4625?**

4624 records successful logons; 4625 records failed logons.

**Q3. What does Event ID 4688 represent?**

It records process creation when process-creation auditing is enabled.

**Q4. Why is event correlation important?**

It connects related events across time and context, helping analysts distinguish normal behavior from activity that may require investigation.

**Q5. Do multiple failed logons prove a brute-force attack?**

No. They may indicate a brute-force attempt, but mistyped passwords, stale credentials, or misconfigured services can also produce failures. Review the source, frequency, accounts, and surrounding events.

